    "result_text": "All changes are complete, the build succeeds, and the test passes. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nDuplicate detection is now a single derived **`identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + householdId`, and a create is rejected with **409 only when a new owner's whole key equals an existing owner's**.\n\n**New files**\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 builds the key: telephone in canonical E.164 form, email lower-cased (empty when absent), householdId (empty when the owner has no household).\n- `OwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 shared household derivation (normalize last name/address, the stable 12-hex id, and a `resolve(...)` that returns the id a request would join or `null` when solo). Used by both the new check and `AssignOwnerHousehold`, so they agree on what a household is.\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the single consolidated check: computes the request's prospective householdId, builds its identityKey, and rejects only on a full-key match against any existing owner.\n- `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateOwnerIdentityExceptionHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2192 responds 409.\n\n**Modified**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 the three steps `ensureUniqueTelephone` / `ensureUniqueEmail` / `ensureUniqueHousehold` are replaced by one `ensureUniqueIdentity` (kept in the same pipeline position, before the city-capacity/daily-limit checks, so error precedence is preserved).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema, so it is returned.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identityKey` via `OwnerIdentityKey.of(owner)`.\n- `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 delegates normalization/id to `OwnerHousehold` (identical derivation).\n- `OwnerAddress.java` \u2014 javadoc updated to point at the new check.\n\n**Deleted** the three old `EnsureUnique*`, `DuplicateOwner*Exception`, `DuplicateOwner*ExceptionHandler` classes and their three escalation YAMLs.\n\n## Behaviour\n\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The acceptance test `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (second owner reusing the first's telephone, no email, no household \u2192 identical key) returns 409.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
